## 8. The Framework's Interpretation

### 8.1 The formula as a sorting function

The formula `m_f(r)` takes a ratio r and returns a value. This value is interpreted as the "processing weight" of the particle at that ratio.

The formula has a maximum at `r = −B/C = 0.055245`, with maximum value 250.11 GeV.

The formula's value is monotone increasing for r < 0.055245 and monotone decreasing for r > 0.055245.

### 8.2 The crossover at kL

The crossover at `m_f = kL` separates particles into two groups: those with processing weight below kL (11 particles) and those above (2 particles: H and t).

### 8.3 The base-2 pattern

The four particles Z, c, d, e sit at ratios where the formula's processing weight equals kL, kL/2, kL/4, kL/8. These are the four cleanest matches to the mesh's hole sizes.

### 8.4 Charge coverage

The four matched particles cover all four Standard Model charge categories: neutral (Z), up-type (+2/3, c), down-type (−1/3, d), charged lepton (−1, e).

